  "title": "Delian League",
  "summary": "In 478 BCE Athens formed the Delian League with Greek city-states, keeping its treasury on Delos; the first tribute assessment is credited to Aristides. Athens moved the treasury to its own city c. 454 BCE after a failed Egyptian expedition, and the league ended in 404 BCE when Athens lost the Peloponnesian War.",
